{"name":"Bright Nori","hex":"#2d5e22","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"nori","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of seaweed, a red alga, laver (genus Pyropia, including species P. yezoensis and P. tenera).","The seaweed, chopped and formed into sheets, used in the preparation of sushi."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of norry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nori"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nori","blocks":[{"text":"Nori (Japanese: 海苔) is a dried edible seaweed used in Japanese cuisine, usually made from species of the red algae genus Pyropia, including P. yezoensis and P. tenera. It has a strong and distinctive flavor, and is generally made into flat sheets and used to wrap rolls of sushi or onigiri."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nori.jpg/330px-Nori.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nori"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Shinagawa_nori_Utagawa_Kuniyoshi_1864.jpg/500px-Shinagawa_nori_Utagawa_Kuniyoshi_1864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Shinagawa_nori_Utagawa_Kuniyoshi_1864.jpg/1280px-Shinagawa_nori_Utagawa_Kuniyoshi_1864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Shinagawa_nori_Utagawa_Kuniyoshi_1864.jpg/500px-Shinagawa_nori_Utagawa_Kuniyoshi_1864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail